      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While it's true that the 2018 patent (US2018/098765) employs a micro-lattice structure for thermal management, the key difference lies in the material used to create the lattice. Our ceramic-based thermal interface material is a game-changer, offering superior thermal conductivity and a more compact form factor compared to the copper structures used in the 2018 patent. Moreover, the lattice design in our patent is not merely a passive structure, but rather an integral component of a proprietary thermal management system that integrates the ceramic material with a novel, patented architecture. This integrated approach ensures a level of thermal performance and efficiency that is not achievable with the copper-based lattice of the 2018 patent.",
      "source": "target",
